{"results":[{"id":"6a33628e05ab2c2a8cced854","name":"Klue Integration Abused in Salesforce Data Theft | Threat Spotlight","description":"In June 2026, a compromised Klue competitive-intelligence platform integration was exploited to exfiltrate customer relationship management data from enterprise Salesforce environments. Attackers authenticated through compromised Klue service accounts, generated OAuth tokens, and executed automated Python scripts to conduct bulk data extraction via Salesforce REST API queries over approximately 24 hours. The activity included concentrated bursts of nearly a thousand queries within 15 minutes and sustained extraction windows exceeding 6 hours. This incident follows similar third-party OAuth-abuse campaigns targeting Salesforce through Salesloft Drift and Gainsight integrations throughout 2025 and 2026. While the tactics resemble operations attributed to ShinyHunters and UNC6395 threat groups, attribution remains uncertain. The initial access vector, full scope of exfiltration, and attacker intent are still under investigation, with no extortion demands observed to date.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-07-18T03:23:58.710000","created":"2026-06-18T03:14:22.763000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[],"tags":["salesforce","unc6395","oauth abuse","api exfiltration","third-party integration","klue integration","shinyhunters","crm data theft"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1213.002","T1119","T1530","T1106","T1567","T1087","T1102","T1528","T1041","T1078","T1567.002","T1059.006","T1213","T1071.001","T1550.001"],"references":["https:\/\/reliaquest.com\/blog\/threat-spotlight-integration-abused-in-crm-data-theft"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a5a11b5327ee76f3502c500","name":"Botnet Analysis: A Product-Grade Threat for the AI Service Era","description":"NadMesh is an industrial-grade Go-based botnet observed in July 2026 that autonomously scans and exploits AI infrastructure and cloud services. The botnet integrates scanning, exploitation, and intelligence harvesting into a single platform targeting over 90 cloud provider address ranges. It employs 20+ exploitation vectors against Redis, Docker, MCP, Kubernetes, and other services, with particular focus on AI platforms like ComfyUI, Ollama, and Gradio discovered via Shodan API. NadMesh features a web-based management panel, polymorphic builds using Garble obfuscation and UPX packing, and redundant persistence mechanisms including SSH backdoors, agent processes, and cron watchdogs. The operation demonstrates clear commercial intent with conversion funnel statistics, canary updates, and automated task supply loops that amplify high-yield subnets. It harvests cloud credentials, Kubernetes tokens, AI model access, and MCP service intelligence.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-07-17T21:16:37.200000","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:49.015000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":644894,"indicator":"CVE-2016-0638","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4439649184,"indicator":"209.99.186.235","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-08-16T11:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4444894790,"indicator":"cdnorigin.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454943029,"indicator":"ca024acead8f54cfe5b07ac4bdf7fcea","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454943030,"indicator":"31c69b3e12936abca770d430066f379ec1d997ec","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454943031,"indicator":"fc4109f5dd1d30b65dd60e57dc639ac1d313bfa5241e36e61fbc4aabc1cda482","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T11:27:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["shodan intelligence","credential harvesting","polymorphic","ai infrastructure targeting","mcp exploitation","botnet","autonomous scanning","go-based","kubernetes compromise","nadmesh","cve-2016-0638"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["NadMesh"],"attack_ids":["T1037","T1133","T1543.003","T1053.003","T1190","T1595.002","T1552.004","T1098.004","T1552.001","T1136.003","T1110","T1027.005","T1078","T1573","T1570","T1095","T1027.002","T1071.001","T1046","T1552.007"],"references":["https:\/\/blog.xlab.qianxin.com\/nadmesh-botnet-analysis-a-product-grade-threat-for-the-ai-service-era-en\/"],"industries":["Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a5a8ba0229db5a5b2686baa","name":"Contagious Interview malware in SVG images: DPRK campaign","description":"A DPRK-aligned threat group is targeting developers through fake job postings and coding challenges in a campaign tracked as REF9403. Attackers post fake job offers in developer forums, then send trojanized repositories containing fully functional e-commerce projects with malicious code hidden using steganography inside SVG flag images. When developers run these projects, the malware deploys four-stage payloads aligned with OTTERCOOKIE: a browser credential and cryptocurrency wallet stealer, a file exfiltration module, a Socket.IO-based remote access trojan, and a clipboard stealer. The campaign was discovered after targeting Elastic's community Slack workspace. Multiple trojanized repositories were found with zero antivirus detections at the time of discovery, demonstrating the sophistication of this supply chain attack vector against software developers.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-07-17T21:11:59.344000","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:00.316000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Contagious Interview","indicators":[{"id":4455079548,"indicator":"3e6360f83a95540aa2176d279ca4694513afb1e5116a7ffe591c6b5bcf3b9c3c","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079549,"indicator":"4e7639045b4a64de60bfb6312951a5c3dffbd3fb04b84837663242ed27f09864","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079550,"indicator":"54bf36910d81ab516037cb3d69d7c85190f90aa0da9e58617799c1fc738dc5a9","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079551,"indicator":"8e571d58794b9b44ae53c2c67bedef72c500e8adbb80aab7a5c263adcba55b1e","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079552,"indicator":"96357529d17c4690826d5d4c74deac51743a5388733b3f04004d898f0635ef20","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079553,"indicator":"9df01d242ef46adfedf8c35cb7cc67b1d27d7dc4a1ce74ab32e984090d579886","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079554,"indicator":"c5aed4c063d4970a03250778da8041da9e0c83d8f22d2f1994da0ad72567ebd9","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079555,"indicator":"cc97517f80f567977300450de11e9a0be53f52657525a20b1091c99fe9e45730","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079556,"indicator":"fb94b2caee2c40635448a98ba0118421e19a400e74ccff73315f8fa42351f53f","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079559,"indicator":"controller.rightwidth.dev","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079560,"indicator":"file.rightwidth.dev","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079561,"indicator":"ldb.rightwidth.dev","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4455079562,"indicator":"upload.rightwidth.dev","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-17T20:08:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["developer targeting","cryptocurrency wallet theft","supply chain attack","svg","ottercookie","steganography","fake job interviews","beavertail","dprk"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["OTTERCOOKIE","BEAVERTAIL"],"attack_ids":["T1113","T1059.007","T1071.004","T1497.001","T1115","T1082","T1005","T1140","T1552","T1555.003","T1083","T1036.004","T1204","T1041","T1059.001","T1027.003","T1189","T1071.001","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/www.elastic.co\/security-labs\/contagious-interview-malware-svg-steganography"],"industries":["Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a5a0f86e175ec219dfa17b2","name":"Behind the Refund: From GST Phishing to Remcos RAT Through a Multi-Stage .NET Infection Chain","description":"A sophisticated phishing campaign targeting Indian businesses and taxpayers leverages GST-related themes to distribute Remcos RAT through a multi-stage .NET framework. Threat actors impersonate Government of India GST communications using fraudulent refund notifications with convincing ARN references. The attack chain begins with a malicious RAR archive containing a .NET executable that employs bitmap-based payload concealment techniques. Through successive stages including Windows Health Optimizer Plus.dll and perfgurd.dll, the malware deploys Remcos RAT entirely in memory, establishing persistence via PowerShell scripts and registry modifications. Command-and-control infrastructure utilizes dynamic DNS services with randomized subdomains under aofmokighoig.hath.network. The deployed Remcos RAT enables remote command execution, keylogging, credential harvesting, file manipulation, and comprehensive system reconnaissance capabilities, representing a financially motivated cybercrime operation specifically t...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-07-17T21:08:32.083000","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:30.007000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4454942805,"indicator":"07d7d21c2c0920d198efb9ea54900a80","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454942806,"indicator":"20476f3a51dfddf3dc0603fc7858d894","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454942807,"indicator":"2a34bdd25b404737ee5d3b52bf0b3b70","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454942808,"indicator":"3757dccb2adae65ccdf8d5e5c948b927","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454942809,"indicator":"7842d12d9e37c75076133be5b9904cb2","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454942810,"indicator":"cc34d9760394104ad47877a0d57e9c63","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-17T11:18:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["bitmap steganography","fileless execution","multi-stage loader","dynamic dns","india targeting","credential theft","gst phishing","remcos rat"],"targeted_countries":["British Indian Ocean Territory","India"],"malware_families":["Remcos RAT"],"attack_ids":["T1113","T1056.001","T1129","T1548.002","T1489","T1204.002","T1566.001","T1082","T1005","T1140","T1555","T1036","T1055","T1218.003","T1021","T1016","T1083","T1057","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1039","T1027","T1071.001","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/www.seqrite.com\/blog\/behind-the-refund-from-gst-phishing-to-remcos-rat-through-a-multi-stage-net-infection-chain\/"],"industries":["Finance","Government"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a32e5873cf59d36f41c77be","name":"ClickFix Campaign Generated Via AI Delivers SmartRAT","description":"In March 2026, threat actors leveraged AI-powered website builders to create typosquatting domains impersonating a Brazilian bank. The campaign employed ClickFix techniques, presenting victims with fake CAPTCHA and BSOD screens to trick them into executing malicious PowerShell commands. This delivered SmartRAT, a PowerShell-based banking trojan with capabilities including encrypted C2 communications, remote control of screen\/keyboard\/mouse, credential theft through keylogging and banking overlays, and QR code interception for transaction fraud. The malware establishes persistence via scheduled tasks and Windows services, and targets Brazilian financial institutions, payment platforms, and cryptocurrency exchanges. The threat actors' C2 panel contained critical authentication flaws allowing client-side bypass, suggesting deployment without adequate security review.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-07-17T18:07:17.865000","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:54.937000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":2590886288,"indicator":"crefisa.online","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4356969737,"indicator":"windowsupdate-cdn.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4383533038,"indicator":"c.windowsupdate-cdn.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376226,"indicator":"297eb45f028d44d750297d2f932b9c91","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376227,"indicator":"3c72e1f37f115b00c3ad6ed31bacfe8a","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376228,"indicator":"6bf4d4c62b5138ace281ce3d08297787","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376229,"indicator":"b17ccdb5531555e43f082d6e77c07227","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376231,"indicator":"http:\/\/64.95.13.238\/payload.php'","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376232,"indicator":"cartaobb.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376233,"indicator":"cartaobrb.com.br","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417376234,"indicator":"vfsgloball.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-17T18:20:55","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["banana rat","fake captcha","smartrat","powershell","typosquatting","ghostloader","brazil","clickfix","qr code interception","banking trojan","credential theft","remcos rat","ai-generated"],"targeted_countries":["Brazil"],"malware_families":["SmartRAT","Banana RAT","Remcos RAT","GhostLoader"],"attack_ids":["T1113","T1056.001","T1543.003","T1082","T1071","T1106","T1005","T1140","T1036","T1055","T1185","T1112","T1059","T1497","T1059.001","T1566","T1027","T1070.004","T1518","T1569.002"],"references":["https:\/\/www.zscaler.com\/blogs\/security-research\/clickfix-campaign-generated-ai-delivers-smartrat"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a59832ac2ebd9e525a462b9","name":"ACR Stealer: Two observed intrusion chains amid increased threat activity","description":"Between late April and mid-June 2026, Microsoft observed heightened ACR Stealer activity targeting enterprise environments through ClickFix social engineering lures. This information-stealing malware, associated with Amatera Stealer rebranding and offered as malware-as-a-service, deployed through two distinct campaigns. The first utilized WebDAV-delivered payloads with Python loaders and blockchain-based command-and-control resolution. The second employed a fileless approach using MSHTA and steganography-concealed payloads within images. Both campaigns harvested browser credentials, authentication tokens, and sensitive documents from compromised systems. Threat actors leveraged obfuscated PowerShell scripts, scheduled task persistence, and in-memory execution techniques to evade detection. Notable tactics included masquerading as legitimate software updates, utilizing Windows DPAPI for credential decryption, and targeting PDF and Microsoft 365 documents. The blockchain dead-drop technique enabled dynamic i...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-07-17T10:44:44.002000","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:38.735000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":2639418634,"indicator":"proton-network.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4348915056,"indicator":"ux.strainedeasily.icu","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4350424591,"indicator":"looksta.icu","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4356970079,"indicator":"fast.raidher.icu","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4367351266,"indicator":"apigrokcloud.icu","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4370017135,"indicator":"deep-harborio.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4378494744,"indicator":"zealpraxis.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454706442,"indicator":"prism-vertex.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454706443,"indicator":"auramatrixa.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4454706444,"indicator":"cpppemwjewjoiwejow.sale","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-17T01:19:39","content":"","title":"","description":